## Detailed Control Mapping (Examples)

### Tenet 1: All Data Sources and Computing Services Are Resources

| 800-53 Control | Control Title | FedRAMP Param | CMMC Practice | ISO 27001 | Evidence Required | ZT Implementation |
|----------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| CM-8 | Component Inventory | Automated discovery, continuous | CM.L2-3.4.9 | A.8.1.1 | CMDB export, discovery scan results, reconciliation report | Automated asset discovery (cloud, on-prem, SaaS), classification tags |
| CM-9 | Configuration Management Plan | Baseline + drift detection | - | A.12.1.2 | Config baselines, drift reports, remediation tickets | IaC, GitOps, drift detection, auto-remediation |
| PM-5 | System Inventory | Enterprise-wide, authoritative | - | A.5.9 | System registry, data flow diagrams, criticality ratings | Service catalog, dependency mapping, business impact analysis |

### Tenet 2: All Communication Is Secured Regardless of Network Location

| 800-53 Control | Control Title | FedRAMP Param | CMMC Practice | ISO 27001 | Evidence Required | ZT Implementation |
|----------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| SC-7 | Boundary Protection | Deny by default, micro-seg | SC.L2-3.13.11 | A.13.1.1 | Network diagrams, firewall rules, segmentation test results | Micro-segmentation, ZTNA, deny-by-default, east-west encryption |
| SC-8 | Transmission Confidentiality/Integrity | TLS 1.3, mTLS everywhere | SC.L2-3.13.12 | A.13.2.1 | Cert inventory, TLS scan results, mTLS verification | mTLS (service mesh), TLS 1.3, certificate automation |
| SC-13 | Cryptographic Protection | FIPS 140-3, key rotation | - | A.10.1.1 | KMS/HSM config, key rotation logs, algorithm certs | CMK, automated rotation, HSM, post-quantum ready |
| SC-23 | Session Authenticity | Mutual auth, binding | - | A.13.2.1 | mTLS config, token binding proof, session logs | SPIFFE, token binding, channel binding |

### Tenet 3: Access Granted on Per-Session Basis

| 800-53 Control | Control Title | FedRAMP Param | CMMC Practice | ISO 27001 | Evidence Required | ZT Implementation |
|----------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| AC-2 | Account Management | Automated lifecycle, JIT | AC.L2-3.1.1 | A.9.2.1 | Provisioning logs, deprovisioning SLA, access review results | HR-driven lifecycle, JIT access, automated deprovisioning |
| AC-3 | Access Enforcement | Dynamic, per-session | AC.L2-3.1.2 | A.9.2.2 | Policy engine logs, decision traces, session records | PDP/PEP, dynamic policy, short-lived sessions |
| AC-12 | Session Termination | Idle timeout, revocation | - | A.9.4.2 | Session logs, revocation tests, timeout config | Short TTL, immediate revocation, continuous eval |
| AC-17 | Remote Access | ZTNA, no VPN, posture | - | A.9.4.3 | ZTNA config, posture checks, access logs | ZTNA, device posture, continuous verification |

### Tenet 4: Access Determined by Dynamic Policy

| 800-53 Control | Control Title | FedRAMP Param | CMMC Practice | ISO 27001 | Evidence Required | ZT Implementation |
|----------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| AC-2 | Account Management | Attribute-based, risk-adaptive | AC.L2-3.1.1 | A.9.1.2 | Policy definitions, attribute sources, decision logs | OPA/Cedar, real-time attributes (risk, posture, threat) |
| AC-3 | Access Enforcement | Fine-grained, context-aware | AC.L2-3.1.3 | A.9.2.3 | AuthZ decisions, obligation logs, break-glass records | ABAC, obligations (step-up, audit), break-glass |
| AC-4 | Information Flow Enforcement | Micro-segmentation, data flow | - | A.9.4.1 | Data flow diagrams, segmentation rules, flow logs | Micro-seg, DLP, data classification, flow control |
| AC-16 | Security/Privacy Attributes | Dynamic labels, classification | - | A.9.4.1 | Label schema, auto-labeling results, label enforcement | Auto-classification, sensitivity labels, policy by label |
| SC-7 | Boundary Protection | Identity-based, not IP-based | SC.L2-3.13.11 | A.13.1.1 | Identity-based rules, policy decision logs | Identity-based micro-seg, zero network trust |

### Tenet 5: Monitor and Measure Integrity and Security Posture

| 800-53 Control | Control Title | FedRAMP Param | CMMC Practice | ISO 27001 | Evidence Required | ZT Implementation |
|----------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| SI-4 | System Monitoring | Real-time, automated response | SI.L2-3.14.1 | A.12.4.1 | Monitoring config, alert rules, response times | EDR/XDR, CSPM, network sensors, UEBA, SOAR |
| SI-7 | Software/Firmware Integrity | Signed artifacts, runtime | SI.L2-3.14.2 | A.12.6.1 | SBOM, signature verification, runtime attestation | Sigstore, admission control, runtime security |
| CM-11 | User-Installed Software | Block unauthorized, allowlist | - | A.12.5.1 | Allowlist, block logs, exception process | Application control, allowlist, container policy |
| RA-5 | Vulnerability Scanning | Continuous, risk-prioritized | RA.L2-3.11.1 | A.12.6.1 | Scan results, remediation SLAs, risk scores | Container scanning, SAST/DAST, prioritized remediation |
| CA-7 | Continuous Monitoring | Automated, dashboard, cATO | - | A.12.4.1 | Monitoring dashboard, control status, POA&M | cATO pipeline, continuous control monitoring |

### Tenet 6: Dynamic Authentication and Authorization

| 800-53 Control | Control Title | FedRAMP Param | CMMC Practice | ISO 27001 | Evidence Required | ZT Implementation |
|----------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| IA-2 | Identification/Authentication (Org Users) | Phishing-resistant MFA | IA.L2-3.5.1 | A.9.3.1 | MFA config, enrollment rates, auth logs | FIDO2/passkeys, conditional access, risk-based |
| IA-3 | Device Identification/Authentication | Certificates, posture | IA.L2-3.5.2 | A.9.4.2 | Device cert inventory, posture API, compliance reports | Device certs, MDM/EDR posture, certificate auth |
| IA-4 | Identifier Management | Unique, lifecycle, federation | - | A.9.3.1 | IdP config, federation trusts, identifier uniqueness | SPIFFE, workload identity, federation |
| IA-5 | Authenticator Management | Rotation, revocation, hardware | IA.L2-3.5.3 | A.9.4.3 | Rotation logs, revocation tests, hardware token inventory | Short-lived certs/tokens, auto-rotation, FIDO2 |
| IA-8 | Non-Local Authentication | ZTNA, no VPN, MFA | - | A.9.4.3 | ZTNA config, MFA enforcement, remote access logs | ZTNA, conditional access, no implicit trust |

